               =20
<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading" id=3D"overview">Overview</h2>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">Betty has many filesystems working together=
 to provide a cohesive storage experience for your research data needs. It =
is important to understand where your data is to understand what to expect.=
 This tutorial provides a brief overview.</p>



<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading" id=3D"home-directories">Home Directories</h2=
>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">Each user gets a HOME directory setup on th=
e <a href=3D"https://parcc.upenn.edu/systems/vast/" data-type=3D"page" data=
-id=3D"26">VAST Filesystem</a> this provides high performance and reliabili=
ty for your most important files such as code repositories, scripts, and co=
nfiguration files.</p>



<figure class=3D"wp-block-table"><table class=3D"has-fixed-layout"><tbody><=
tr><td>Location</td><td>/vast/home/&lt;first letter of PennKey&gt;/&lt;Penn=
Key&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>Quota Size</td><td>50GB</td></tr><tr><td>Quota INo=
des</td><td>250,000</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">Users must be careful, if the HOME director=
y is filled users may not be able to connect. HOME directories have bi-week=
ly snapshots, but we highly recommend keeping a copy of these files elsewhe=
re such as GitHub, Google Drives, or your laptop.</p>



<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading" id=3D"vast-projects">VAST Projects</h2>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph"><a href=3D"https://parcc.upenn.edu/systems/=
vast/" data-type=3D"page" data-id=3D"26">VAST is a high performance flash f=
ile system</a>. Users are strongly encouraged to read/write to this file sy=
stem if your application is heavily dependent on I/O of you users expect hi=
gh performance processing (large amounts of data). VAST storage is organize=
d into projects in <a href=3D"https://parcc.upenn.edu/training/faculty-info=
/coldfront/" data-type=3D"training" data-id=3D"480">Coldfront</a>.</p>



<figure class=3D"wp-block-table"><table class=3D"has-fixed-layout"><tbody><=
tr><td>Location</td><td>/vast/projects/&lt;PI-PennKey&gt;/&lt;project name&=
gt;</td></tr><tr><td>Quota Size</td><td># GB</td></tr><tr><td>Quota INodes<=
/td><td># GB * 5000</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>



<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading" id=3D"ceph-projects">Ceph Projects</h2>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph"><a href=3D"https://parcc.upenn.edu/systems/=
ceph/" data-type=3D"page" data-id=3D"28">Ceph is a distributed filesystem c=
onfigured with HDDs and a small front end NVMe cache</a>. This is designed =
for =E2=80=9Clong term storage file system=E2=80=9D. Users should place fil=
es that are not active (accessed by computing jobs) on this file system.</p=
>



<figure class=3D"wp-block-table"><table class=3D"has-fixed-layout"><tbody><=
tr><td>Location</td><td>/ceph/projects/&lt;PI-PennKey&gt;/&lt;project name&=
gt;</td></tr><tr><td>Quota Size</td><td># GB</td></tr><tr><td>Quota INodes<=
/td><td># GB * 500</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>



<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading" id=3D"local-scratch">Local Scratch</h2>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">Compute nodes have a modest amount of local=
 scratch that can be used if fast I/O is needed. It is located in /tmp</p>



<figure class=3D"wp-block-table"><table class=3D"has-fixed-layout"><tbody><=
tr><td>Location</td><td>/tmp/$USER</td></tr><tr><td>Shared Size</td><td>~50=
0GB</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">From a compute node, you can make a folder =
in the local scratch space.</p>



<pre class=3D"wp-block-code" style=3D"position: relative;"><code>mkdir /tmp=
/$USER</code><button class=3D"copy-button" aria-label=3D"Copy code to clipb=
oard" type=3D"button"><i class=3D"fa-light fa-copy" aria-hidden=3D"true"></=
i></button></pre>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">Once your compute is done ensure you copy t=
he data and remove from the local scratch.</p>



<pre class=3D"wp-block-code" style=3D"position: relative;"><code>cp -r /tmp=
/$USER &lt;project or home folder&gt;
rm -r /tmp/$USER</code><button class=3D"copy-button" aria-label=3D"Copy cod=
e to clipboard" type=3D"button"><i class=3D"fa-light fa-copy" aria-hidden=
=3D"true"></i></button></pre>

